// The harness.v1 sidecar wire. A skill step becomes a session in a harness,
// and the mill drives that harness through an adapter: a child process
// spawned per step and spoken to over newline-delimited JSON on stdio. This
// file types both ends of that pipe. docs/architecture.md §"Skill steps: the
// harness adapter" is its rationale; the Go adapter and the TypeScript
// sidecar are both generated from here, so neither side hand-writes a frame.
//
// Encoding. One protojson-encoded Request or Response per line, no framing
// beyond the newline. Every message therefore has to survive a JSON
// round-trip with no side channel: there are no bytes fields and no
// well-known types beyond Struct, whose JSON is its own value.
//
// This package defines no service. The transport is a pipe, not Connect; a
// unix socket with Connect is the upgrade if a sidecar ever has to outlive
// its worker, and nothing in MVP needs that.

